{"id": "EUVD-2026-98701", "enisaUuid": "d155a103-adda-33a1-827a-8beeba94fab2", "description": "FreeRDP 3.0.0-beta4 before 3.32.0 contains a NULL pointer dereference in arm_handle_request_ok when an ARM endpoint returns an empty HTTP 200 body. Attackers controlling the configured ARM gateway can return a zero-length body to pass NULL to strnlen and crash the connecting client.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T12:07:32", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/FreeRDP/FreeRDP/security/advisories/GHSA-qjwp-c855-hc69", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/freerdp-3.0.0-beta4-before-3.32.0-null-pointer-crash-via-arm-response"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109679", "GHSA-w7w2-8hr6-7gcf"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f1a6f474-1b93-3ac8-9883-11a7b0691e1e", "product": {"name": "FreeRDP", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}, "product_version": "3.0.0-beta4 <3.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b4fc07f6-35cd-33f3-8354-08bfd21f29b7", "vendor": {"name": "FreeRDP"}}], "isExploited": false}